# Backticked `/token`s in shipped documents that are NOT skill invocations.
# Read by conformance/test-documented-skills.py. Format: `token<TAB>reason`.
#
# WHY A DECLARATION AND NOT A HEURISTIC. A shipped document writes `/health` and
# `/repo-review` identically, and no amount of pattern-matching separates an HTTP
# route from a slash-command reliably. So the exemptions are NAMED, each with a
# written reason -- the form V5C-110 permits -- rather than guessed at.
#
# THE FAIL DIRECTION: forgetting to declare a route here produces a FALSE POSITIVE,
# which is loud and takes one line to fix. A heuristic that guessed wrong would
# produce SILENCE, which is how ten dangling skill references shipped for eight cuts.
health	the L.7 version-stamped liveness/readiness contract; the single most-cited endpoint in this package
ready	a readiness probe route, paired with /health in the go-live checks
version	a build-identity route named beside /health
deploy	a directory in the repository layout (`/deploy/**`), a DevOps-owned contract surface per K.10
tmp	a filesystem path in shell examples
schedule	an example application route in the permission matrix
v2	an example public API contract version, used to show what may not change without an ADR
skill	the literal placeholder in the control roster's own description of `documented-skills` -- "a document telling a reader to type a `/skill` that does not exist". HARVEST-CONTEXT.md is GENERATED from that description, so the control quoting itself tripped itself. Not a route and not an invocation: no skill will ever be named `skill`

